m...[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m...[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m...[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m...[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◒[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◐[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◓[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[35m◑[39m  [38;5;209mWaiting for agent reply…[39m.[1G[J[32m◇[39m  \r\n[?25h\r[2KI’m pulling the fuller article text now so the final JSON has enough raw material and better factual density.\r\nI’m grabbing the full Cointelegraph piece too, so the final raw content isn’t just a feed snippet.\r\n{\r\n  \"topic_theme\": \"CLARITY Act passes Senate Banking Committee and sparks bullish crypto sentiment\",\r\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"CLARITY Act\",\r\n  \"primary_headline\": \"CLARITY Act clears Senate Banking Committee, lifting Bitcoin sentiment and crypto markets\",\r\n  \"sources_used\": [\r\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\r\n    \"Decrypt\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"source_urls\": [\r\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-clarity-act-brings-major-spike-of-euphoria-to-bitcoin-santiment\",\r\n    \"https://decrypt.co/367946/morning-minute-the-clarity-act-just-passed-its-first-major-vote\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\r\n    \"Decrypt reported the CLARITY Act cleared the Senate Banking Committee in a 15-9 bipartisan vote, with every Republican voting yes and Democrats Ruben Gallego and Angela Alsobrooks crossing over.\",\r\n    \"Cointelegraph reported Bitcoin was trading at $79,084 and said Santiment measured 1.55 bullish social media comments on Bitcoin for every bearish one, warning that crowded optimism can be a contrarian signal.\",\r\n    \"Decrypt said BTC hit $82,000 on the vote, while Circle rose 19.9% and Coinbase gained 6.1%; prediction markets lifted the odds of the bill passing to 70%.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"The biggest crypto news event across the feeds was the CLARITY Act advancing through the Senate Banking Committee and triggering a strong reaction across Bitcoin, crypto equities, and sentiment trackers.\\n\\nDecrypt’s Morning Minute said the CLARITY Act cleared the Senate Banking Committee on Thursday in a 15-9 bipartisan vote. Every Republican voted yes, and two Democrats crossed over: Ruben Gallego of Arizona and Angela Alsobrooks of Maryland. The vote came after late-night negotiations collapsed without a deal on ethics provisions. Decrypt quoted Senator Cynthia Lummis saying there was agreement on 99% of the bill and that the remaining 1% should be resolved after the bill leaves committee. It also noted that Angela Alsobrooks said her committee yes vote did not guarantee support on the floor unless the ethics language is addressed.\\n\\nDecrypt said markets reacted immediately. Bitcoin hit $82,000 on the vote. Circle surged 19.9%, Coinbase gained 6.1%, and prediction market odds of passage rose 8% to 70%. The piece framed the vote as a major step forward, but still not a final victory. The bill must still clear the full Senate, where it needs 60 votes, meaning roughly six Democratic crossovers. After that, it would need House reconciliation with the version passed 294-134 in July 2025, before any presidential signature. Lummis warned that missing this window could delay the next viable legislative opportunity until 2030.\\n\\nCointelegraph focused on how the vote and the surrounding policy momentum affected Bitcoin sentiment. It reported that Bitcoin was trading at $79,084 at the time of publication, up 3.15% since May 1 according to CoinMarketCap. The article cited Santiment saying there were 1.55 bullish social media comments on Bitcoin for every bearish comment, and that this bullish skew may be a warning sign because markets often move opposite the crowd’s expectations. Santiment explicitly advised caution. Even so, the article said crypto analysts were upbeat about the legislative shift. MN Trading Capital founder Michael van de Poppe called the legislation “the biggest, and historical, bill for the entire industry” and said it could be a strong trigger for the next bull market. White House crypto advisor Patrick Witt said the CLARITY Act vote was a major step forward, but not yet finalized, and that more work was needed before the bill would be ready for prime time.\\n\\nCointelegraph also said Santiment views movement toward passage as bullish over the long run because it could give the industry clearer rules in the United States. The article quoted Santiment saying that if the CLARITY Act passes, more institutional money and powerful players would be expected to enter or re-enter the market. At the same time, it warned that much of that upside could already be priced in before final passage. The piece added a broader sentiment backdrop: the Crypto Fear & Greed Index posted a Fear score of 31 on Saturday.\\n\\nTaken together, the two sources tell a consistent story: the CLARITY Act became the main policy catalyst for crypto, especially Bitcoin, after a major Senate committee vote. The immediate market response was stronger in Decrypt’s reporting, where BTC briefly touched $82,000 and related crypto equities rallied, while Cointelegraph emphasized that sentiment had turned euphoric enough to raise contrarian caution flags. The bill is not yet law, but both sources frame it as one of the most important crypto policy developments of the period because it could define clearer U.S. rules for digital assets and potentially open the door to more institutional participation.\\n\\nRaw article details from Cointelegraph: Bitcoin’s move was linked to the CLARITY Act’s legislative momentum, with Santiment tracking 1.55 bullish comments for every bearish one. The article highlighted that even though the legislation may be bullish structurally, market psychology can overshoot. It also referenced the broader market mood through the Fear & Greed Index, which remained in Fear territory at 31. The article’s central tension was that policy progress can support long-term adoption while also creating short-term crowding.\\n\\nRaw article details from Decrypt: the Senate Banking Committee vote was 15-9, bipartisan, and came despite unresolved ethics language. Decrypt listed the top market movers immediately after the vote: BTC at $82,000, Circle up 19.9%, Coinbase up 6.1%, and the bill’s passage odds at 70%. It laid out the next legislative steps clearly: full Senate, then House reconciliation, then the president. It also emphasized that this was a first major vote, not final passage, so the news event is best understood as a significant policy advance rather than a completed regulatory overhaul.\\n\\nOverall, the primary event is the CLARITY Act’s Senate Banking Committee breakthrough and its direct impact on Bitcoin sentiment and crypto market pricing.\"\r\n} CHART_COIN: bitcoin","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778916963161}}
{"type":"message","id":"91fef2e0","parentId":"11799bbb","timestamp":"2026-05-16T07:36:32.407Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"✅ Research done, starting article..."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_begLlyrgHy6VGjEimn1fpHwt","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/research.json","content":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"CLARITY Act passes Senate Banking Committee and sparks bullish crypto sentiment\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"CLARITY Act\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"CLARITY Act clears Senate Banking Committee, lifting Bitcoin sentiment and crypto markets\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-clarity-act-brings-major-spike-of-euphoria-to-bitcoin-santiment\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/367946/morning-minute-the-clarity-act-just-passed-its-first-major-vote\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Decrypt reported the CLARITY Act cleared the Senate Banking Committee in a 15-9 bipartisan vote, with every Republican voting yes and Democrats Ruben Gallego and Angela Alsobrooks crossing over.\",\n    \"Cointelegraph reported Bitcoin was trading at $79,084 and said Santiment measured 1.55 bullish social media comments on Bitcoin for every bearish one, warning that crowded optimism can be a contrarian signal.\",\n    \"Decrypt said BTC hit $82,000 on the vote, while Circle rose 19.9% and Coinbase gained 6.1%; prediction markets lifted the odds of the bill passing to 70%.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"The biggest crypto news event across the feeds was the CLARITY Act advancing through the Senate Banking Committee and triggering a strong reaction across Bitcoin, crypto equities, and sentiment trackers.\\n\\nDecrypt’s Morning Minute said the CLARITY Act cleared the Senate Banking Committee on Thursday in a 15-9 bipartisan vote. Every Republican voted yes, and two Democrats crossed over: Ruben Gallego of Arizona and Angela Alsobrooks of Maryland. The vote came after late-night negotiations collapsed without a deal on ethics provisions. Decrypt quoted Senator Cynthia Lummis saying there was agreement on 99% of the bill and that the remaining 1% should be resolved after the bill leaves committee. It also noted that Angela Alsobrooks said her committee yes vote did not guarantee support on the floor unless the ethics language is addressed.\\n\\nDecrypt said markets reacted immediately. Bitcoin hit $82,000 on the vote. Circle surged 19.9%, Coinbase gained 6.1%, and prediction market odds of passage rose 8% to 70%. The piece framed the vote as a major step forward, but still not a final victory. The bill must still clear the full Senate, where it needs 60 votes, meaning roughly six Democratic crossovers. After that, it would need House reconciliation with the version passed 294-134 in July 2025, before any presidential signature. Lummis warned that missing this window could delay the next viable legislative opportunity until 2030.\\n\\nCointelegraph focused on how the vote and the surrounding policy momentum affected Bitcoin sentiment. It reported that Bitcoin was trading at $79,084 at the time of publication, up 3.15% since May 1 according to CoinMarketCap. The article cited Santiment saying there were 1.55 bullish social media comments on Bitcoin for every bearish comment, and that this bullish skew may be a warning sign because markets often move opposite the crowd’s expectations. Santiment explicitly advised caution. Even so, the article said crypto analysts were upbeat about the legislative shift. MN Trading Capital founder Michael van de Poppe called the legislation “the biggest, and historical, bill for the entire industry” and said it could be a strong trigger for the next bull market. White House crypto advisor Patrick Witt said the CLARITY Act vote was a major step forward, but not yet finalized, and that more work was needed before the bill would be ready for prime time.\\n\\nCointelegraph also said Santiment views movement toward passage as bullish over the long run because it could give the industry clearer rules in the United States. The article quoted Santiment saying that if the CLARITY Act passes, more institutional money and powerful players would be expected to enter or re-enter the market. At the same time, it warned that much of that upside could already be priced in before final passage. The piece added a broader sentiment backdrop: the Crypto Fear & Greed Index posted a Fear score of 31 on Saturday.\\n\\nTaken together, the two sources tell a consistent story: the CLARITY Act became the main policy catalyst for crypto, especially Bitcoin, after a major Senate committee vote. The immediate market response was stronger in Decrypt’s reporting, where BTC briefly touched $82,000 and related crypto equities rallied, while Cointelegraph emphasized that sentiment had turned euphoric enough to raise contrarian caution flags. The bill is not yet law, but both sources frame it as one of the most important crypto policy developments of the period because it could define clearer U.S. rules for digital assets and potentially open the door to more institutional participation.\\n\\nRaw article details from Cointelegraph: Bitcoin’s move was linked to the CLARITY Act’s legislative momentum, with Santiment tracking 1.55 bullish comments for every bearish one. The article highlighted that even though the legislation may be bullish structurally, market psychology can overshoot. It also referenced the broader market mood through the Fear & Greed Index, which remained in Fear territory at 31. The article’s central tension was that policy progress can support long-term adoption while also creating short-term crowding.\\n\\nRaw article details from Decrypt: the Senate Banking Committee vote was 15-9, bipartisan, and came despite unresolved ethics language. Decrypt listed the top market movers immediately after the vote: BTC at $82,000, Circle up 19.9%, Coinbase up 6.1%, and the bill’s passage odds at 70%. It laid out the next legislative steps clearly: full Senate, then House reconciliation, then the president. It also emphasized that this was a first major vote, not final passage, so the news event is best understood as a significant policy advance rather than a completed regulatory overhaul.\\n\\nOverall, the primary event is the CLARITY Act’s Senate Banking Committee breakthrough and its direct impact on Bitcoin sentiment and crypto market pricing.\"\n}\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":40216,"output":2403,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":42619,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778916963163,"responseId":"chatcmpl-Dg3r3zJTFZyCW82J9dVWLgbyoxQ4A"}}
