reply…...[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…...[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply…[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◑  Waiting for agent reply….[1G[J◒  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◐  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◓  Waiting for agent reply…..[1G[J◇  \n[?25hMETA\n- SEO Title: CLARITY Act | Coinography Market Reaction Guide\n- Meta Description: See how the CLARITY Act vote moved Bitcoin, Coinbase, and Circle, and track the key price and sentiment signals traders should watch next.\n- URL Slug: clarity-act-senate-committee-bitcoin-sentiment\n- Categories: Bitcoin News, Policy, Latest News\n- Primary Keyword: CLARITY Act\n- Secondary Keywords: Bitcoin sentiment, crypto market reaction\n\n# CLARITY Act lifts Bitcoin sentiment as BTC nears $82,000\n\nCLARITY Act momentum gave traders a fresh policy catalyst after the bill cleared the Senate Banking Committee in a 15-9 bipartisan vote. Bitcoin briefly touched $82,000 after the result, putting US regulation back at the center of price action.\n\nThe crypto market reaction spread beyond BTC. Circle rose 19.9%, Coinbase added 6.1%, and prediction markets pushed passage odds to 70%, showing traders quickly repriced the chance of clearer US rules.\n\nThis looks like policy repricing, not a clean trend confirmation.\n\n## Bitcoin sentiment: What the CLARITY Act vote signals\n\nThe vote mattered because it moved the CLARITY Act out of committee and into a more visible stage. [According to Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/367946/morning-minute-the-clarity-act-just-passed-its-first-major-vote), every Republican backed the bill, while Democrats Ruben Gallego and Angela Alsobrooks crossed over to support it.\n\nThat fed directly into Bitcoin sentiment. [Cointelegraph reported](https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-clarity-act-brings-major-spike-of-euphoria-to-bitcoin-santiment) that Santiment tracked 1.55 bullish Bitcoin comments for every bearish one, though Alsobrooks also said her committee vote did not guarantee support on the Senate floor.\n\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n### Bipartisan support changes the setup\n\nCommittee approval does not make the bill law, but it clears one major hurdle. The next steps are a full Senate vote with a 60-vote threshold, reconciliation with the House version passed in July 2025, and then a presidential signature.","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778917229470}}
