{"type":"message","id":"6dac2afd","parentId":"dab016c9","timestamp":"2026-05-16T07:40:45.777Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Current step: Step 2 — Write.\nThe previous writer run completed, but validation shows the saved file contains terminal progress noise mixed into the article, which inflated the word count and would break publishing.\nI will rerun the writer cleanly without PTY, then revalidate the saved markdown before proceeding to Step 2.5."},{"type":"text","text":"The draft came back with terminal noise mixed into the file, so I’m doing a clean recovery run now before moving on."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0qAiLmyfXGkBZtP4o0HetC5S","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"rm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/writer/sessions/sessions.json\nRESEARCH_JSON=$(cat /tmp/research.json)\nopenclaw agent --agent writer --message \"First, read the COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md file in your workspace to learn your strict formatting rules. Then, write a 1100-1200 word crypto news article using these facts: $RESEARCH_JSON. You MUST finish the article completely, ending with the Sources and Word Count block.\" --deliver > /tmp/crypto-article-raw.txt\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nraw = Path('/tmp/crypto-article-raw.txt').read_text(errors='ignore')\nstart = raw.find('META')\nif start == -1:\n    start = raw.find('# ')\nclean = raw[start:] if start != -1 else raw\nPath('/tmp/crypto-article.md').write_text(clean)\nprint('START_INDEX', start)\nprint('HAS_WORD_COUNT', 'Word Count:' in clean)\nprint('WORDS', len(clean.split()))\nprint('LINES', len(clean.splitlines()))\nprint('---PREVIEW---')\nprint('\\n'.join(clean.splitlines()[:35]))\nPY","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator","yieldMs":120000,"timeout":1800,"pty":false}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":20415,"output":937,"cacheRead":52864,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":74216,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778917229473,"responseId":"chatcmpl-Dg3vMTmBWXY7KJ1Vk5jSyJQGAi3sl"}}
{"type":"message","id":"9acdf298","parentId":"6dac2afd","timestamp":"2026-05-16T07:41:44.251Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0qAiLmyfXGkBZtP4o0HetC5S","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"START_INDEX 0\nHAS_WORD_COUNT True\nWORDS 1327\nLINES 99\n---PREVIEW---\nMETA\n- SEO Title: CLARITY Act | Coinography Market Analysis\n- Meta Description: Track how the CLARITY Act vote moved Bitcoin sentiment, BTC price action, and crypto stocks, then see the key levels traders should watch.\n- URL Slug: clarity-act-senate-banking-committee-bitcoin-sentiment\n- Categories: Bitcoin News, Latest News\n- Primary Keyword: CLARITY Act\n- Secondary Keywords: Bitcoin sentiment, crypto market reaction, BTC price levels\n\n# CLARITY Act lifts Bitcoin sentiment as BTC taps $82,000 after 15-9 vote\n\nCLARITY Act momentum turned into a live market catalyst after the bill cleared the Senate Banking Committee in a 15-9 bipartisan vote. Bitcoin briefly hit $82,000 on the headline, while the broader market treated the committee advance as a sign that US crypto rules may finally be moving toward a clearer framework.\n\nThe reaction was not limited to BTC. Circle jumped 19.9%, Coinbase gained 6.1%, and prediction markets pushed the odds of full passage up to 70%, [according to Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/367946/morning-minute-the-clarity-act-just-passed-its-first-major-vote). At the same time, social chatter around Bitcoin turned notably bullish, which can support price in the short run but also raise crowding risk.\n\nThis is not a final policy win. It is a sharp repricing event tied to a serious legislative step.\n\n## Bitcoin sentiment: What It Means After the Committee Vote\n\nThe committee result matters because it gives traders a concrete policy milestone instead of another headline about possible reform. Decrypt reported that every Republican on the committee backed the bill, with Democrats Ruben Gallego and Angela Alsobrooks also voting yes, even though ethics language remains unresolved. That mix of bipartisan support and unfinished negotiation is why the move looks constructive, but not complete.\n\nFor Bitcoin sentiment, the bigger takeaway is that policy progress is now being priced as a medium-term adoption signal. [Cointelegraph reported](https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-clarity-act-brings-major-spike-of-euphoria-to-bitcoin-santiment) that Santiment measured 1.55 bullish Bitcoin comments for every bearish one. That is a strong skew, and Santiment also warned that when optimism gets crowded, markets often move against the consensus.\n\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n### Bipartisan support changed the market narrative\n\nBefore this vote, the CLARITY Act was mainly a policy story. After the vote, it became a trading input. The market is starting to treat regulatory clarity as something that can affect capital flows, exchange valuations, and institutional positioning.\n\nThat shift showed up fast in multiple places:\n- Bitcoin touched $82,000 immediately after the vote\n- Circle rallied 19.9% and Coinbase rose 6.1%\n- Prediction market odds of passage climbed to 70%\n\nThe reason this matters is simple. A bill moving through committee reduces uncertainty, even if it does not eliminate it. Traders usually price progress before final passage, not after."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":58457,"aggregated":"START_INDEX 0\nHAS_WORD_COUNT True\nWORDS 1327\nLINES 99\n---PREVIEW---\nMETA\n- SEO Title: CLARITY Act | Coinography Market Analysis\n- Meta Description: Track how the CLARITY Act vote moved Bitcoin sentiment, BTC price action, and crypto stocks, then see the key levels traders should watch.\n- URL Slug: clarity-act-senate-banking-committee-bitcoin-sentiment\n- Categories: Bitcoin News, Latest News\n- Primary Keyword: CLARITY Act\n- Secondary Keywords: Bitcoin sentiment, crypto market reaction, BTC price levels\n\n# CLARITY Act lifts Bitcoin sentiment as BTC taps $82,000 after 15-9 vote\n\nCLARITY Act momentum turned into a live market catalyst after the bill cleared the Senate Banking Committee in a 15-9 bipartisan vote. Bitcoin briefly hit $82,000 on the headline, while the broader market treated the committee advance as a sign that US crypto rules may finally be moving toward a clearer framework.\n\nThe reaction was not limited to BTC. Circle jumped 19.9%, Coinbase gained 6.1%, and prediction markets pushed the odds of full passage up to 70%, [according to Decrypt](https://decrypt.co/367946/morning-minute-the-clarity-act-just-passed-its-first-major-vote). At the same time, social chatter around Bitcoin turned notably bullish, which can support price in the short run but also raise crowding risk.\n\nThis is not a final policy win. It is a sharp repricing event tied to a serious legislative step.\n\n## Bitcoin sentiment: What It Means After the Committee Vote\n\nThe committee result matters because it gives traders a concrete policy milestone instead of another headline about possible reform. Decrypt reported that every Republican on the committee backed the bill, with Democrats Ruben Gallego and Angela Alsobrooks also voting yes, even though ethics language remains unresolved. That mix of bipartisan support and unfinished negotiation is why the move looks constructive, but not complete.\n\nFor Bitcoin sentiment, the bigger takeaway is that policy progress is now being priced as a medium-term adoption signal. [Cointelegraph reported](https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-clarity-act-brings-major-spike-of-euphoria-to-bitcoin-santiment) that Santiment measured 1.55 bullish Bitcoin comments for every bearish one. That is a strong skew, and Santiment also warned that when optimism gets crowded, markets often move against the consensus.\n\n[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]\n\n### Bipartisan support changed the market narrative\n\nBefore this vote, the CLARITY Act was mainly a policy story. After the vote, it became a trading input. The market is starting to treat regulatory clarity as something that can affect capital flows, exchange valuations, and institutional positioning.\n\nThat shift showed up fast in multiple places:\n- Bitcoin touched $82,000 immediately after the vote\n- Circle rallied 19.9% and Coinbase rose 6.1%\n- Prediction market odds of passage climbed to 70%\n\nThe reason this matters is simple. A bill moving through committee reduces uncertainty, even if it does not eliminate it. Traders usually price progress before final passage, not after.","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778917304251}}
