  <skill>\\n    <name>clawhub</name>\\n    <description>Search, install, update, sync, or publish agent skills with the ClawHub CLI and registry.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/clawhub/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>coding-agent</name>\\n    <description>Delegate feature work, PR review, refactors, or iterative coding to background Codex, Claude Code, or Pi agents.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/coding-agent/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>gog</name>\\n    <description>Google Workspace CLI for Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Contacts, Sheets, and Docs.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/gog/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>healthcheck</name>\\n    <description>Audit and harden hosts running OpenClaw for SSH, firewall, updates, exposure, cron checks, and risk posture.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/healthcheck/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>mcporter</name>\\n    <description>List, configure, authenticate, call, and inspect MCP servers/tools with mcporter over HTTP or stdio.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/mcporter/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>node-connect</name>\\n    <description>Diagnose OpenClaw Android, iOS, or macOS node pairing, QR/setup code, route, auth, and connection failures.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/node-connect/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>skill-creator</name>\\n    <description>Create, edit, improve, tidy, review, audit, or restructure AgentSkills and SKILL.md files.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>taskflow</name>\\n    <description>Coordinate multi-step detached tasks as one durable TaskFlow job with owner context, state, waits, and child tasks.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/taskflow/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>taskflow-inbox-triage</name>\\n    <description>Example TaskFlow pattern for inbox triage, intent routing, waiting on replies, and later summaries.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/taskflow-inbox-triage/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>tmux</name>\\n    <description>Remote-control tmux sessions for interactive CLIs by sending keystrokes and scraping pane output.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/tmux/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>video-frames</name>\\n    <description>Extract frames or short clips from videos using ffmpeg.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/video-frames/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>weather</name>\\n    <description>Get current weather, rain, temperature, and forecasts for locations or travel planning.</description>\\n    <location>~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/weather/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n</available_skills>\",","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778918127732}}
{"type":"message","id":"2dadff60","parentId":"2801ae1f","timestamp":"2026-05-16T07:55:27.734Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1XtZ53rnwsnHsnzZxnEU5gC6","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"chart_refs 2\nfeature_refs 0\n23 ![Bitcoin Price Chart](/tmp/chart.png)\n48 ![Bitcoin Price Chart](/tmp/chart.png)"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":102,"aggregated":"chart_refs 2\nfeature_refs 0\n23 ![Bitcoin Price Chart](/tmp/chart.png)\n48 ![Bitcoin Price Chart](/tmp/chart.png)","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778918127732}}
{"type":"message","id":"2c841e65","parentId":"2dadff60","timestamp":"2026-05-16T07:55:36.965Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found the gap — the article file does contain the chart, but the WordPress publish step was only set up to carry over the feature image."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7tsMjUii9wqHwYhZwaXyPvrO","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh","offset":1,"limit":260}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_CGWY9Pyd5uTcmgtG3Jkbn8bc","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/SOUL.md","offset":1,"limit":140}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":118288,"output":342,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":118630,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778918127740,"responseId":"chatcmpl-Dg49qFse8azHkT4IlMEOngopthghP"}}
{"type":"message","id":"55c91fff","parentId":"2c841e65","timestamp":"2026-05-16T07:55:36.993Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7tsMjUii9wqHwYhZwaXyPvrO","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# =============================================================================\n# publish.sh — WordPress Publishing Skill for Scribe (wp-publisher agent)\n# =============================================================================\n# Usage:\n#   bash publish.sh [--title \"Title\"] [--excerpt \"Excerpt\"]\n#                  [--article /path/to/article.md] [--image /path/to/image.jpg]\n#\n# Smart extraction: reads SEO Title, Meta Description, URL Slug directly from\n# the Writer's META block in the article — no manual passing needed.\n#\n# Pipeline cleanup: strips META block, Word Count line, and thinking blocks\n# before publishing so only clean article content reaches WordPress.\n#\n# Output:\n#   Exit 0 → /tmp/wp-result.txt contains the WordPress draft post URL\n#   Exit 1 → /tmp/wp-error.log  contains the human-readable error reason\n# =============================================================================\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# --- Config ------------------------------------------------------------------\nWP_URL=\"https://slateblue-reindeer-775070.hostingersite.com\"\nWP_API=\"${WP_URL}/wp-json/wp/v2\"\nWP_USER=\"spearmintmarketingpro@gmail.com\"\nWP_PASS=\"B1u0 7AQI Aw5a IQK7 0KWX PtGU\"\nCATEGORY_ID=3\nPOST_STATUS=\"draft\"\n\nARTICLE_PATH=\"/tmp/crypto-article.md\"\nIMAGE_PATH=\"/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg\"\nCLEAN_MD=\"/tmp/crypto-article-clean.md\"\nHTML_PATH=\"/tmp/crypto-article.html\"\nRESULT_FILE=\"/tmp/wp-result.txt\"\nERROR_FILE=\"/tmp/wp-error.log\"\nMAX_RETRIES=3\n\n# --- Argument Parsing --------------------------------------------------------\nTITLE=\"\"\nEXCERPT=\"\"\n\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --title)   TITLE=\"$2\";   shift 2 ;;\n    --excerpt) EXCERPT=\"$2\"; shift 2 ;;\n    --article) ARTICLE_PATH=\"$2\"; shift 2 ;;\n    --image)   IMAGE_PATH=\"$2\";   shift 2 ;;\n    *) shift ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\n# --- Helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------\nlog_info()  { echo \"[INFO]  $*\"; }\nlog_error() { echo \"[ERROR] $*\" | tee -a \"$ERROR_FILE\"; }\nfatal()     { log_error \"$*\"; exit 1; }\n\n# --- Setup -------------------------------------------------------------------\nrm -f \"$ERROR_FILE\" \"$RESULT_FILE\" \"$CLEAN_MD\" \"$HTML_PATH\" /tmp/wp-meta.txt\n\nif [ ! -f \"$ARTICLE_PATH\" ]; then\n  fatal \"Article not found at '$ARTICLE_PATH'. Has the Writer agent run yet?\"\nfi\n\n# =============================================================================\n# PHASE 0: Extract metadata from META block + produce clean article\n# =============================================================================\nlog_info \"Parsing article — extracting metadata and stripping pipeline internals...\"\n\npython3 - <<PYEOF\nimport re\n\nwith open(\"${ARTICLE_PATH}\", \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    raw = f.read()\n\n# --- Extract META block values -----------------------------------------------\nmeta_title = \"\"\nmeta_desc  = \"\"\nmeta_slug  = \"\"\n\nmeta_match = re.search(r'^META\\b(.*?)^---', raw, re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL)\nif meta_match:\n    block = meta_match.group(1)\n    t = re.search(r'[-*]\\s*SEO Title:\\s*(.+)',          block)\n    d = re.search(r'[-*]\\s*Meta Description:\\s*(.+)',   block)\n    s = re.search(r'[-*]\\s*URL Slug:\\s*(.+)',           block)\n    if t: meta_title = t.group(1).strip()\n    if d: meta_desc  = d.group(1).strip()\n    if s: meta_slug  = s.group(1).strip().lower()\n\nwith open(\"/tmp/wp-meta.txt\", \"w\") as mf:\n    mf.write(\"META_TITLE=\" + meta_title + \"\\n\")\n    mf.write(\"META_DESC=\"  + meta_desc  + \"\\n\")\n    mf.write(\"META_SLUG=\"  + meta_slug  + \"\\n\")\n\n# --- Strip pipeline-internal content from article ----------------------------\nclean = raw\n\n# 1. Remove META block (from line starting with \"META\" to first \"---\")\nclean = re.sub(r'^META\\b.*?^---[ \\t]*\\n', '', clean, count=1, flags=re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL)\n\n# 2. Remove <thinking>...</thinking> blocks\nclean = re.sub(r'<thinking>.*?</thinking>', '', clean, flags=re.DOTALL | re.IGNORECASE)\n\n# 3. Remove Word Count line in any format: \"Word Count: 1,198\" or \"[Word Count: 1198]\"\nclean = re.sub(r'^\\[?Word Count:.*?\\]?\\s*$', '', clean, flags=re.MULTILINE | re.IGNORECASE)\n\n# 4. Collapse more than 2 consecutive blank lines into 1\nclean = re.sub(r'\\n{3,}', '\\n\\n', clean)\n\nclean = clean.strip() + \"\\n\"\n\nwith open(\"${CLEAN_MD}\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    f.write(clean)\n\nprint(\"[INFO]  META block extracted:\")\nprint(f\"[INFO]    SEO Title:        {meta_title[:70]}\")\nprint(f\"[INFO]    Meta Description: {meta_desc[:80]}\")\nprint(f\"[INFO]    URL Slug:         {meta_slug}\")\nprint(f\"[INFO]  Clean article written to ${CLEAN_MD}\")\nPYEOF\n\n# --- Read extracted meta into bash -------------------------------------------\nEXTRACTED_TITLE=\"\"\nEXTRACTED_DESC=\"\"\nEXTRACTED_SLUG=\"\"\n\nif [ -f /tmp/wp-meta.txt ]; then\n  while IFS='=' read -r key value; do\n    case \"$key\" in\n      META_TITLE) EXTRACTED_TITLE=\"$value\" ;;\n      META_DESC)  EXTRACTED_DESC=\"$value\"  ;;\n      META_SLUG)  EXTRACTED_SLUG=\"$value\"  ;;\n    esac\n  done < /tmp/wp-meta.txt\n  rm -f /tmp/wp-meta.txt\nfi\n\n# --- Resolve final title (CLI → META block → H1 → date fallback) -------------\nif [ -z \"$TITLE\" ]; then\n  if [ -n \"$EXTRACTED_TITLE\" ]; then\n    TITLE=\"$EXTRACTED_TITLE\"\n    log_info \"Title source: META block SEO Title\"\n  else\n    TITLE=$(grep -m 1 \"^# \" \"$CLEAN_MD\" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/^# //' || echo \"\")\n    [ -z \"$TITLE\" ] && TITLE=\"Crypto News - $(date +%Y-%m-%d)\"\n    log_info \"Title source: H1 heading (META block not found)\"\n  fi\nfi\n\n# --- Resolve final excerpt (CLI → META description → first 3 body lines) -----\nif [ -z \"$EXCERPT\" ]; then\n  if [ -n \"$EXTRACTED_DESC\" ]; then\n    EXCERPT=\"$EXTRACTED_DESC\"\n    log_info \"Excerpt source: META block Meta Description\"\n  else\n    EXCERPT=$(grep -v \"^#\" \"$CLEAN_MD\" 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"^[[:space:]]*$\" | \\\n              head -3 | tr '\\n' ' ' | sed 's/[[:space:]]\\+/ /g' | cut -c1-300 || echo \"\")\n    log_info \"Excerpt source: first body paragraphs\"\n  fi\nfi\n\nSLUG=\"$EXTRACTED_SLUG\"\n\nlog_info \"Final Title:   $TITLE\"\nlog_info \"Final Slug:    ${SLUG:-<WordPress auto-generate>}\"\nlog_info \"Post Status:   $POST_STATUS | Category ID: $CATEGORY_ID\"\n\n# =============================================================================\n# PHASE 1: Upload Featured Image\n# =============================================================================\nMEDIA_ID=0\n\nif [ -f \"$IMAGE_PATH\" ]; then\n  FILE_SIZE=$(stat -c%s \"$IMAGE_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f%z \"$IMAGE_PATH\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\n  if [ \"$FILE_SIZE\" -gt 51200 ]; then\n    log_info \"Uploading featured image ($FILE_SIZE bytes)...\"\n\n    MEDIA_RESPONSE=$(curl --silent --write-out \"\\n__STATUS__%{http_code}\" \\\n      --user \"${WP_USER}:${WP_PASS}\" \\\n      --request POST \"${WP_API}/media\" \\\n      --header \"Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=crypto-feature.jpg\" \\\n      --header \"Content-Type: image/jpeg\" \\\n      --data-binary @\"$IMAGE_PATH\" \\\n      --max-time 60)\n\n    MEDIA_BODY=$(echo \"$MEDIA_RESPONSE\" | sed '$d')\n    MEDIA_STATUS=$(echo \"$MEDIA_RESPONSE\" | tail -1 | sed 's/__STATUS__//')\n    log_info \"Image upload: HTTP $MEDIA_STATUS\"\n\n    if [ \"$MEDIA_STATUS\" = \"201\" ] || [ \"$MEDIA_STATUS\" = \"200\" ]; then\n      MEDIA_ID=$(echo \"$MEDIA_BODY\" | python3 -c \\\n        \"import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin).get('id', 0))\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)\n      log_info \"Image uploaded. Media ID: $MEDIA_ID\"\n    elif [ \"$MEDIA_STATUS\" = \"401\" ] || [ \"$MEDIA_STATUS\" = \"403\" ]; then\n      log_error \"Image upload auth error (HTTP $MEDIA_STATUS). Proceeding without image.\"\n    else\n      log_error \"Image upload failed (HTTP $MEDIA_STATUS). Proceeding without featured image.\"\n    fi\n  else\n    log_error \"Image file too small ($FILE_SIZE bytes). Skipping.\"\n  fi\nelse\n  log_info \"No image at '$IMAGE_PATH'. Publishing without featured image.\"\nfi\n\n# =============================================================================\n# PHASE 1.5: Upload Chart Image & Embed\n# =============================================================================\nCHART_PATH=\"/tmp/chart.png\"\nif [ -f \"$CHART_PATH\" ]; then\n  log_info \"Uploading chart image...\"\n  CHART_RESPONSE=$(curl --silent --write-out \"\\n__STATUS__%{http_code}\" \\\n    --user \"${WP_USER}:${WP_PASS}\" \\\n    --request POST \"${WP_API}/media\" \\\n    --header \"Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=chart.png\" \\\n    --header \"Content-Type: image/png\" \\\n    --data-binary @\"$CHART_PATH\" \\\n    --max-time 60)\n\n  CHART_BODY=$(echo \"$CHART_RESPONSE\" | sed '$d')\n  CHART_STATUS=$(echo \"$CHART_RESPONSE\" | tail -1 | sed 's/__STATUS__//')\n\n  if [ \"$CHART_STATUS\" = \"201\" ] || [ \"$CHART_STATUS\" = \"200\" ]; then\n    CHART_URL=$(echo \"$CHART_BODY\" | python3 -c \"import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin).get('source_url', ''))\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"\")\n    if [ -n \"$CHART_URL\" ]; then\n      log_info \"Chart uploaded. URL: $CHART_URL\"\n      python3 -c \"\nwith open('${CLEAN_MD}', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f: content = f.read()\ncontent = content.replace('[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]', '<img src=\\\"${CHART_URL}\\\" alt=\\\"Crypto Price Chart\\\"/>')\nwith open('${CLEAN_MD}', 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f: f.write(content)\n\"\n    fi\n  else\n    log_error \"Chart upload failed (HTTP $CHART_STATUS). Proceeding without chart.\"\n  fi\nelse\n  log_info \"No chart generated at '$CHART_PATH'.\"\nfi\n\n# =============================================================================\n# PHASE 2: Convert Clean Markdown → HTML\n# =============================================================================\nlog_info \"Converting clean article to HTML...\"\n\nif command -v pandoc &>/dev/null; then\n  if pandoc \"$CLEAN_MD\" -t html -o \"$HTML_PATH\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    log_info \"Pandoc conversion successful.\"\n  else\n    log_error \"Pandoc failed. Using raw content fallback.\"\n    cp \"$CLEAN_MD\" \"$HTML_PATH\"\n  fi\nelse\n  log_error \"Pandoc not installed. Using raw markdown as content.\"\n  cp \"$CLEAN_MD\" \"$HTML_PATH\"\nfi\n\n# =============================================================================\n# PHASE 3: Create WordPress Post (with retry + exponential backoff)\n# =============================================================================\nlog_info \"Creating WordPress draft post (max $MAX_RETRIES attempts)...\"\n\n[113 more lines in file. Use offset=261 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778918136993}}
{"type":"message","id":"f5077bb3","parentId":"55c91fff","timestamp":"2026-05-16T07:55:36.993Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_CGWY9Pyd5uTcmgtG3Jkbn8bc","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md — Scribe, the WordPress Publisher\n\nYou are **Scribe** 🗞️, the WordPress publisher agent for a crypto news pipeline. You are called by the Orchestrator (Nexus) after the human has confirmed they want the article published to WordPress.\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL RULES — READ BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE\n\n1. **You have a `bash` tool. You MUST USE IT.** Do not describe what you would do. Execute the actual commands below.\n2. **NEVER invent or guess a WordPress URL.** The only valid success output is what `cat /tmp/wp-result.txt` prints after the script exits 0.\n3. **Every step marked `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]` must produce a real bash execution.** No exceptions.\n4. **Do not ask questions.** The article and image are already on disk. Just publish.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1 — Publish to WordPress `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]`\n\n<thinking>\nThe article is at /tmp/crypto-article.md and the image is at /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg.\nI will now run the publish script. The script will auto-extract the title and excerpt from the article file — I do not need to pass them unless the message explicitly provides them.\nI will execute the bash tool right now.\n</thinking>\n\nRun this **exact** command using your bash tool:\n\n```bash\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh\n```\n\nIf the Orchestrator's message includes an explicit article title, pass it:\n\n```bash\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-wp-publisher/skills/wordpress/publish.sh --title \"TITLE FROM MESSAGE\"\n```\n\n**WAIT for the script to finish. Do NOT skip this step. Do NOT guess the output.**\n\nThe script handles everything: image upload, HTML conversion, WordPress API call, retries, and validation.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2 — Read the Result `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]`\n\n<thinking>\nThe script has finished. I will check the exit code and read the appropriate output file.\n</thinking>\n\n**If the script exited with code `0` (success):**\n```bash\ncat /tmp/wp-result.txt\n```\nThis prints the live WordPress draft post URL. Return it exactly.\n\n**If the script exited with code `1` (failure):**\n```bash\ncat /tmp/wp-error.log\n```\nReturn exactly: `WP_FAILED: <contents of the error log>`\n\n---\n\n## Step 3 — Final Output\n\nReturn ONLY one of these two things:\n- The WordPress post URL (e.g. `https://slateblue-reindeer-775070.hostingersite.com/?p=123`)\n- Or: `WP_FAILED: <reason from error log>`\n\n**No extra commentary. No explanation. No apology. Just the result.**\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778918136993}}
{"type":"message","id":"cd44dcc2","parentId":"f5077bb3","timestamp":"2026-05-16T07:55:49.535Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Yes — I found the exact bug.\n\n**What happened**\n- The article file already had the chart embedded as `![Bitcoin Price Chart](/tmp/chart.png)` in **2 places**.\n- But the WordPress publish script only knows how to upload the chart and replace **`[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]`**.\n- Since I had already replaced the placeholder earlier, the script never rewrote those `/tmp/chart.png` links to a real WordPress media URL.\n\n**Result**\n- The draft post ended up pointing at a local temp path (`/tmp/chart.png`), which WordPress can’t serve, so the chart is missing.\n\n**In short:** this is a pipeline bug, not a chart-generation bug.\n\nI can fix it two ways:\n1. **Patch the publisher script** so future posts include charts correctly, then create a corrected draft.  \n2. **Fix just this article once** and republish a corrected draft.\n\nI recommend **option 1**. If you want, I’ll do it."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":4019,"output":737,"cacheRead":118144,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":122900,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778918136999,"responseId":"chatcmpl-Dg4A0hc5GnJ3chg29rHw2lf36Ggyj"}}
